{
  "_doc": "What a thing is WORTH, as a multiplier on its class price (economy.merchant_price; ECONOMY_REFACTOR_PROPOSAL D4). A trader's price follows the item's real worth, not only its class: a Potion of Sickness is junk and Full Healing is dear. Stock stays unidentified, so a sharp player can price-identify (a NetHack-style discovery). The hero SELLS an item as what he knows it as: a thing whose type is unknown is priced as its unidentified class (worth 1, tier 2), so selling never leaks a name. Lookup order: 'by_id', then 'by_effect' for the item's class, then 1.0. 'share_by_id' replaces the class share outright for a thing no class fits (a pet egg). Uniques also take economy.UNIQUE_GEAR_SHARE / UNIQUE_ACCESSORY_SHARE.",
